WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
If your prep is SUPREP, this video will walk you through exactly how to

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.060
take it.

3
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.320
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.860
Your bowel prep kit comes with two small bottles and a mixing container.

5
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.200
You'll use one bottle the evening before your procedure and the second bottle

6
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.220
the morning of.

7
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.860
You'll also need water.

8
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.860
For your first dose, between 5 and 6 PM the evening before your colonoscopy,

9
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.100
pour the entire contents of the first bottle into the mixing container provided

10
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:25.360
.

11
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.760
Fill the container with water to the 16-ounce fill line and drink the entire

12
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.320
amount.

13
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.890
After you finish, continue to drink 16 to 32 ounces of clear liquids until you

14
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:35.600
go to bed.

15
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.840
Remember, do not drink red, orange, blue or purple liquids.

16
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.280
For your second dose, 7 hours before your procedure time,

17
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.640
pour the entire contents of the second bottle into the mixing container.

18
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.800
Fill with water to the 16-ounce fill line and drink the entire amount.

19
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.230
After finishing this second dose, drink an additional 32 ounces of water within

20
00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.080
one hour.

21
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.160
Do not have any liquids at all within 4 hours of your procedure.

22
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.660
This part is really important.

23
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.860
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

24
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.160
passing clear liquid.

25
00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.840
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

26
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.740
the clearest view during your procedure.

27
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.890
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

28
00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:21.960
of us wants that.

29
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.040
Staying hydrated throughout the process is key.

30
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.800
Make sure you're drinking plenty of clear liquids between your doses.

31
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.840
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

32
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.500
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

33
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.180
That's it, you've got this.

34
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.700
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

35
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.660
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

36
00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:49.620
We're here to help.
